course: dictionary
lesson: 6792
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the sentence around the word tells you which one the writer means. The word orchestra is a good example. Its main meaning is a large group of musicians who play many instruments together. «Before an orchestra plays, the players tune up.» Here, the players are the musicians, so orchestra means the whole group.
explain: The word can also name a place in a theatre. «The orchestra stalls are the seats at the front on the ground floor.» Stalls are seats, so this orchestra means the seats, not the musicians. Ask yourself what would fit: could the people sit there? Yes, so this is the seating meaning.
explain: Look for clues in the words around the word. «Orchestras usually seat the quieter strings at the front and the louder brass and percussion at the back.» Strings, brass and percussion are all types of instrument, so orchestra here means the musicians who play them. When you find a word with more than one meaning, test each meaning in the sentence and keep the one that makes sense.
fact: An orchestra is a large group of musicians who play many instruments together.
fact: Orchestras are often split into sections: strings, woodwind, brass and percussion.
fact: «Before a concert the orchestra tunes to one note, usually an A played by the oboe.»
fact: The orchestra pit is the low space in front of a stage where the orchestra plays.
fact: In the UK, the orchestra stalls are the front seats on the ground floor of a theatre.
exercise: «Before an orchestra plays, the players tune up.» What is an orchestra here? | *A large group of musicians who play many instruments together | A single person who plays the oboe | A stage for plays
exercise: «The orchestra stalls are the seats at the front on the ground floor.» Where are the orchestra stalls? | At the back of a school hall | On the stage, behind the singers | *In a theatre, at the front on the ground floor
exercise: «Orchestras usually seat the quieter strings at the front and the louder brass and percussion at the back.» Copy one word that names a section of the orchestra. | front | seat | louder | *brass
test: «Before a concert the orchestra tunes to one note, usually an A played by the oboe.» Why does the orchestra tune up? | So the audience can dance | To make the concert end sooner | *So everyone plays in tune together | To hide the sound of the oboe
test: «The orchestra pit is the low space in front of a stage where the orchestra plays.» Where is the orchestra pit? | Outside the building | *Low down, in front of the stage | On top of the stage | At the top of the theatre
exam: Which sentence uses orchestra to mean a group of musicians? | The orchestra stalls were full of families | *The school orchestra played a lovely piece at the concert | The orchestra was a loud, fast car | Our orchestra is the name of a sweet shop
